A wait that ends leaves its thread lending.
A thread that runs again still pays for its borrower's turns.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a thread that does not wait lends

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@ static void unwait(struct thread *t)
 {
     ring_remove(&((struct notification *)p2v(t->waiting_on))->waiters, t);
     t->waiting_on = 0;
-    if (t->lend_to != 0) {
+    if (t->lend_to != 0 && t->waiting_on != 0) {
         unlend(t);
     }
 }
